        <type>std::vector&lt; SgFunctionDeclaration * &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt; SgFunctionDeclaration * &gt; CallTargetSet::solveFunctionPointerCall</definition>
        <argsstring>(SgPointerDerefExp *)</argsstring>
        <name>solveFunctionPointerCall</name>
        <param>
          <type>SgPointerDerefExp *</type>
          <defname>pointerDerefExp</defname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Finds all functions that match the function type of pointerDerefExp. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="namespaceCallTargetSet_1ab913177c8199b292422d3b668ba5cd56" kindref="member">CallTargetSet::solveFunctionPointerCall</ref></para><para>Resolving function pointer calls is hard, so the <ref refid="classCallGraph" kindref="compound">CallGraph</ref> generator doesn&apos;t try very hard at it. When asked to resolve a function pointer call, it simply finds all functions that match that type in the memory pool a returns a list of them.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">pointerDerefExp</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>: <ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref> function pointer dereference. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>: <ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref> vector of all functionDeclarations that match the type of the function dereferenced in pointerDerefExp </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
